      "text": "To determine the value of \\( n \\) for which the number \\( 712n \\) is divisible by 18, we need to check two conditions: divisibility by 2 and divisibility by 9. \n\n1. **Divisibility by 2**: Since \\( 712n \\) ends in \\( n \\), it is already divisible by 2, regardless of the value of \\( n \\).\n\n2. **Divisibility by 9**: A number is divisible by 9 if the sum of its digits is divisible by 9. So, we need the sum of the digits \\( 7 + 1 + 2 + n \\) to be divisible by 9.\n\nWe can set up the equation:\n\\[ 7 + 1 + 2 + n = 10 + n \\]\n\nNow we need to find the value of \\( n \\) such that \\( 10 + n \\) is divisible by 9.\n\nLet's write a Python script to find the correct value of \\( n \\).\n\n```python\n# We need to find n such that 10 + n is divisible by 9\nn = 0\nwhile True:\n    if (10 + n) % 9 == 0:\n        break\n    n += 1\n\nprint(n)\n```\n```output\n8\n```\nThe value of \\( n \\) that makes the four-digit number \\( 712n \\) divisible by 18 is \\( \\boxed{8} \\).",
